# Deepfathom Echo: "At the beginning of combat on your turn, this creature explores. Then you may have it become a copy of another
# creature you control until end of turn." Turn 1: it explores a Mox Emerald (a +1/+1 counter), which Bot1 puts into the graveyard
# this time (CR 701.44a), and Bot1 declines to copy the Ornithopter. Turn 3: with the beginning-of-combat trigger on the stack Bot2
# exiles the 5/5 Echo with Swords to Plowshares (Bot1 gains 5, its power as it last was). The trigger still resolves and explores
# without it (CR 701.44c: the Plains goes to Bot1's hand, no counter can be put anywhere), but there is nothing to become a copy:
# Bot1 is not asked which creature, though it has an Ornithopter (a wrong implementation would still ask).

